    <div class="subject">REQUEST FOR SABBATICAL LEAVE: ACADEMIC YEAR 2025-2026</div>

    <div class="greeting">Dear Professor Martinez,</div>

    <div class="content">
        <p>I am writing to formally request a sabbatical leave for the Fall semester of the 2025-2026 academic year. Having served as a faculty member for the past seven years, I am eligible for this sabbatical. This leave would significantly enhance my academic contribution to the department and the field.</p>

        <p>During my sabbatical, I plan to complete my book manuscript, "<em>Borders in Translation: Literary Migrations Across the Global South</em>," which examines cross-cultural identity formation. This builds upon research supported by the university's Faculty Research Grant (2023) and a fellowship (2024).</p>

        <div class="sabbatical-plan">
            <h3>Sabbatical Research Plan</h3>
            <p>My sabbatical project will involve:</p>
            <ol class="timeline">
                <li><strong>Manuscript Completion:</strong> Finalizing three chapters of my book manuscript, solicited by Duke University Press.</li>
                <li><strong>Archival Research:</strong> Conducting a research visit to the National Library of Brazil.</li>
                <li><strong>International Collaboration:</strong> Working with colleagues at the University of São Paulo on our digital humanities project.</li>
            </ol>

            <p>This will contribute to our department's emphasis on global literary movements and enhance graduate course offerings upon my return.</p>
        </div>

        <p>Professor Anna Kim has agreed to serve as interim advisor to my doctoral students, and Professor James Wong will cover my World Literature seminar (CL301). I will complete committee work before departure and remain available virtually.</p>

        <p>Upon my return, I will offer a new graduate seminar, "Literary Border-Crossings in the Global South," and plan to organize a symposium to foster international scholarly exchange.</p>

        <p>Thank you for considering this request. I am happy to provide any additional information.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="closing">Respectfully submitted,</div>

